// BUG FIXED 2026-08-03: this was 240s with horaKey() quantised to 96 steps, so the whole
// world re-baked its palette every 2.5s and every colour in the frame stepped at once —
// measured at 5.29 rgb levels per pixel on average, 9.24 at worst. A global colour step
// twice per five seconds is not ambience, it is a strobe, and the owner read it exactly as
// that: "o fundo tá com um efeito estranho, meio bugado se mexendo".
// Two changes, because slowing the clock alone only makes the same jump rarer: the turn is
