// ---------- THE RHYTHM, AS WEATHER ----------
// GO FAST and GO STEADY rendered pixel-identical frames: the one decision this prototype
// exists to measure had no consequence you could SEE. It does now, and it is weather, not
// a colour grade — the air in front of a world being pushed is thick, hot and full of
// cinders, and the air in front of a world being tended is clear and full of living things.
//
// Three rules keep it from taking the picture over:
//   · the sick→healed arc stays dominant. The rhythm only ever adds warm haze, and it adds
//     it IN PROPORTION TO THE DISTANCE EACH PLANE ALREADY CARRIES — the near plane barely
//     moves, the horizon takes most of it. That is aerial perspective thickening, the
